uw_replay - offline UW-fail characterization harness
====================================================

Answers: among Iridium bursts that PASS burst_downmix correlation but FAIL the
qpsk_demod unique-word re-check (the "_UN" population, ~37% on the Elba feeder),
which factor is responsible and what fraction is actually recoverable?

It replays the EXACT qpsk_demod decode logic against saved post-downmix burst
frames (.cf32, 250 kHz / 10 sps, extracted at the correlator's uw_start) and
sweeps one recovery knob at a time: 4-quadrant phase rotation, symbol-timing /
start-phase, and residual CFO (+/-40 kHz). A full-frame exhaustive UW slide
answers "is the DL/UL unique word present ANYWHERE in this burst?"

Built-in oracle: baseline must PASS the _DL files and FAIL the _UN files. If it
reproduces those ground-truth labels, the replay is faithful.

Only dependency is ../iridium.h (repo root). No FFTW, no CMake. Keep this file
in tests/ so the include resolves.

BUILD
-----
    gcc -O2 -o tests/uw_replay tests/uw_replay.c -lm

RUN
---
    tests/uw_replay <corpus_dir> [max_files]

  <corpus_dir>  directory of *_DL.cf32 / *_UL.cf32 / *_UN.cf32 files
                (wherever --save-bursts wrote them)
  max_files     process at most this many (0/absent = all). Use it to avoid
                waiting hours on a 100k+ corpus.

  Env toggles:
    UW_NO_SCAN=1   skip the exhaustive full-frame UW slide (~25 ms/file). Turn
                   OFF for a fast pass, keep ON for the definitive pass.
    UW_VERBOSE=1   force the per-file table (auto-suppressed above 200 files).

TYPICAL SESSION
---------------
    # fast representative pass, summary only:
    UW_NO_SCAN=1 tests/uw_replay <corpus_dir> 5000

    # definitive pass with full-frame UW slide on a smaller subsample:
    tests/uw_replay <corpus_dir> 2000

READING THE OUTPUT
------------------
  BASELINE fidelity   DL should be ~100% pass, UN ~0% pass. If not, the replay
                      is not matching production for that batch - investigate
                      before trusting anything else.
  recovery by knob    how many UN reach UW Hamming<=2 under each single knob.
                      rotation/start-phase ~0 => alignment is NOT the problem.
                      CFO>0 => residual-Doppler subset (fix in burst_downmix.c
                      estimate_fine_cfo, NOT qpsk_demod.c).
  UW found somewhere  UN with the UW present at any alignment. Low => most UN
                      are not standard-UW frames (likely burst-detector false
                      positives; correlate_sync has no acceptance threshold).

CAVEAT
------
A 12-symbol UW can match by chance across a wide CFO sweep. Treat "recoveries"
as candidates until confirmed by DOWNSTREAM decode (BCH/CRC actually passing).

Reference sample sits in ./burst_sample (20 DL + 20 UN). See
RESEARCH_NOTE_UW_FAIL_CHARACTERIZATION.md (top correction block) for findings.
